<article class="env-lemma" id="0710">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0710">Lemma <span data-tag="0710">18.38.1</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{O})$ be a ringed site. Let $p$ be a point of $\mathcal{C}$. Let $U$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$. For $\mathcal{G}$ in $\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (j_{U!}\mathcal{G})_ p = \bigoplus \nolimits _ q \mathcal{G}_ q  \]
</div>
  <p> where the coproduct is over the points $q$ of $\mathcal{C}/U$ lying over $p$, see Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/04H3" data-tag="04H3">7.35.2</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We use the description of $j_{U!}\mathcal{G}$ as the sheaf associated to the presheaf $V \mapsto \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi \in \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {C}(V, U)} \mathcal{G}(V/_\varphi U)$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/03DI" data-tag="03DI">18.19.2</a>. The stalk of $j_{U!}\mathcal{G}$ at $p$ is equal to the stalk of this presheaf, see Lemma <a href="/tag/04EQ" data-tag="04EQ">18.36.3</a>. Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \textit{Sets}$ be the functor corresponding to $p$ (see Sites, Section <a href="/tag/00Y3" data-tag="00Y3">7.32</a>). Hence we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (j_{U!}\mathcal{G})_ p = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{(V, y)} \bigoplus \nolimits _{\varphi : V \to U} \mathcal{G}(V/_\varphi U)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       where the colimit is taken in the category of abelian groups. To a quadruple $(V, y, \varphi , s)$ occurring in this colimit, we can assign $x = u(\varphi )(y) \in u(U)$. Hence we obtain 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (j_{U!}\mathcal{G})_ p = \bigoplus \nolimits _{x \in u(U)} \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{(\varphi : V \to U, y), \  u(\varphi )(y) = x} \mathcal{G}(V/_\varphi U).  \]
</div>
    <p>
       This is equal to the expression of the lemma by the description of the points $q$ lying over $x$ in Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/04H3" data-tag="04H3">7.35.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>